From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vcds-on-mac <peter@vcds-on-mac.local>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:50:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Handle macOS Apple Silicon W^X for mixed code+data
 host pages.

macOS on arm64 hard-enforces W^X: mprotect(PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC) always
fails with EACCES (no entitlement bypasses it for plain mappings).

This breaks PE images with 4K section alignment (VCDS-ARM.exe among
them) on 16K host pages: a single host page can contain both code and
data 4K pages, and Wine merges per-page protections with a union over
the host page (get_host_page_vprot), yielding rwx requests.  The result
was a failed mprotect during map_image_into_view, leaving the image's
.text/.data boundary page read-exec, and any write to data on that page
raised a stuck access violation (VCDS spun forever in exception
dispatch at 100% CPU).

Fix it like write-watches: degrade rwx to rw- in mprotect_exec, and flip
the host page between read-write and read-exec on demand from
virtual_handle_fault (exec fault -> r-x, write fault -> rw-).  Both
flips return STATUS_SUCCESS so execution continues transparently.

With this, VCDS-ARM.exe boots its full process tree (services.exe,
explorer.exe with the winemac Cocoa loop, conhost.exe) and idles
waiting on the desktop window handshake.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 994a8dee..448156e1 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1603,6 +1603,18 @@ static inline int mprotect_exec( void *base, size_t size, int unix_prot )
         if (!(unix_prot & PROT_WRITE)) return -1;
     }
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+    /* macOS on Apple Silicon enforces W^X: write+exec mappings always fail.
+     * This matters for PE images with 4K section alignment, where a single
+     * 16K host page can contain both code and data pages whose protections
+     * get merged.  Degrade to read-write and let virtual_handle_fault flip
+     * the page to read-exec on an instruction fetch (and back on a write). */
+    if ((unix_prot & (PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC)) == (PROT_WRITE | PROT_EXEC))
+    {
+        TRACE( "degrading w^x protection on %p-%p\n", base, (char *)base + size - 1 );
+        return mprotect( base, size, unix_prot & ~PROT_EXEC );
+    }
+#endif
     return mprotect( base, size, unix_prot );
 }
 
@@ -4336,7 +4348,26 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *data, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec,
             if ((vprot & VPROT_WRITEWATCH) || is_write_watch_range( page, 1 ))
                 ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         }
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+        /* W^X-degraded host page (mixed code+data, see mprotect_exec):
+         * the page is currently read-exec, flip it back to read-write */
+        if (ret && is_vprot_exec_write( vprot ) &&
+            (get_unix_prot( get_page_vprot( addr )) & PROT_WRITE))
+        {
+            if (!mprotect( page, host_page_size, get_unix_prot( vprot ) & ~PROT_EXEC ))
+                ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
+#endif
+    }
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+    else if (err == EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_FAULT && is_vprot_exec_write( vprot ) &&
+             (get_page_vprot( addr ) & VPROT_EXEC))
+    {
+        /* W^X-degraded host page currently read-write: flip it to read-exec */
+        if (!mprotect( page, host_page_size, get_unix_prot( vprot ) & ~PROT_WRITE ))
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
     }
+#endif
     mutex_unlock( &virtual_mutex );
     rec->ExceptionCode = ret;
     return ret;
-- 
